# Tony's Pizza Fantasy — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Never commit `.env.local`.
#
# Three environments exist, and they must never share a database:
#
#   local       Docker (or a local cluster) — `npm run db:up`
#   preview     the Neon SANDBOX branch — every pull request deploys here
#   production  the Neon PRODUCTION branch — the live *.vercel.app URL
#
# Vercel Hobby preview URLs are public-by-URL, so a preview pointed at
# production data would publish the league's records to anyone holding a link
# (`17 §10`). Scope the preview `DATABASE_URL` to the sandbox branch and never
# to production.
#
# See `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` for the provisioning runbook.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — REQUIRED
#
# Local development and tests run against a local Postgres, never a hosted
# database (`16 §11`), so tests are offline, free, and cannot reach production.
#
#   npm run db:up          start local Postgres
#   npm run db:migrate     apply migrations
#   npm run sleeper:import import the league chain from recorded fixtures
#   npm run db:down        stop and DELETE the volume
#
# Running the import twice should report zero records changed the second
# time — a re-sync is a no-op by design.
#
# In production and preview this points at Neon. Use Neon's POOLED connection
# string (the host containing `-pooler`) in serverless environments so the
# pool cannot exhaust connections.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=postgres://tonys:local_dev_only@localhost:5432/tonys_dev

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sessions — REQUIRED once authentication is deployed.
#
# Signs the 90-day rolling session cookie. A different value per environment,
# so a preview cookie can never be replayed against production.
#
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Rotating this signs every existing manager out. That is the intended
# emergency response, not a routine operation.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sleeper — no credentials required; the API is public and read-only.
# The league ID is configuration, not a secret.
#
# This is the CURRENT season's league ID. Sleeper mints a new one each year;
# earlier seasons are reached by following `previous_league_id` backwards, so
# only the newest ID is ever configured. The chain currently reads
# 2026 -> 2025 -> 2024 and terminates there.
#
# Only `npm run sleeper:record` reads the live API. Application code and the
# test suite read the committed fixtures in `fixtures/sleeper/`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SLEEPER_LEAGUE_ID=1385016656425668608

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The commissioner — configuration, not a secret.
#
# The Sleeper user ID that holds admin rights: PIN resets, and later the Slice
# review screen and the time machine. Admin is granted by `npm run db:seed`
# from this value, so it is version-controlled configuration rather than a
# database row somebody set by hand and cannot account for.
#
# Unset means NOBODY is an admin and every admin route 404s. That is the safe
# default, not a broken one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# COMMISSIONER_SLEEPER_USER_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tony's Tuesday Slice — optional.
#
# The Slice MUST publish correctly with this unset (16 §9). The template
# renderer is the default path; the model is a second renderer the
# commissioner may choose per story. Leaving this blank is a supported
# production configuration, not a degraded one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scheduled jobs — shared secret for the two protected cron routes
# (Sunday pre-Monday snapshot, Tuesday finalize). Not yet built.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRON_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absolute origin — deliberately UNSET and deliberately unused.
#
# Nothing in the application knows its own URL: session cookies are host-only,
# links are relative, and no artifact embeds an origin. That is what lets a
# `juncaj.net` subdomain be attached later as a Vercel setting plus a DNS
# record, with no code change (`17 §10`).
#
# The first feature that genuinely needs an absolute URL — a share link, an
# email — reads it from here. Until then, adding it would only create a value
# that can drift out of date without anything noticing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP_ORIGIN=
